Problem:
Expand $(2x^5 + 3x^2)(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8)$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to expand the expression:

\begin{align*}
(2x^5 + 3x^2)(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) &= 2x^5(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) + 3x^2(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) \\
&= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 6x^6 - 16x^5 + 3x^6 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2 \\
&= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2.
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2}$.
====================

