Problem:
Evaluate $(1+2i)6-3i$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to expand the product:

\begin{align*}
(1+2i)(6-3i) &= 1\cdot6 + 1\cdot(-3i) + 2i\cdot6 + 2i\cdot(-3i) \\
&= 6 - 3i + 12i - 6i^2 \\
&= 6 - 3i + 12i + 6(-1) \\
&= 6 - 3i + 12i - 6 \\
&= 0 + 9i \\
&= \boxed{9i}.
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $9i$. I hope it is correct.
